# DIM — Dial In Master

## Purpose

Measure how easy a coffee is to dial in and keep producing excellent shots.

DIM becomes one of BigShotEspresso's signature metrics.

### DIM Factors

- Shots until first reference shot
- Reference shot percentage
- Grind drift required
- Rating consistency
- Aging stability
- Fault frequency

### Example

DIM 90–100

- Extremely forgiving
- Easy to dial in
- Easy to repeat

DIM 70–89

- Good everyday coffee

DIM 50–69

- Requires attention

DIM below 50

- Finicky
- Advanced users only

---

# GSP — Great Shot Potential

## Purpose

Measure how good a coffee can become when everything goes right.

DIM asks:

"How easy is it?"

GSP asks:

"How high can it go?"

Example:

Coffee A

DIM 92
GSP 80

Coffee B

DIM 42
GSP 98

Coffee B may be difficult but capable of producing extraordinary shots.

